# Headings

Sizes come from `admin/src/assets/layout/_typography.scss` (the UI scale), largest first:

| Level | Use | Size |
|-------|-----|------|
| `h1` | Page title (`app-page`, public form pages) — one per page | 22px (`.page-title`) |
| `h2` | Card / panel title: `<h2 class="card-title">` | 14px via `.card-title` (bare h2 17px) |
| `h3` | Sub-section inside a card (e.g. "More links", "Score areas") | 14px |
| `h4` | Minor heading under an h3 | 13px |

- Go h1 → h2 → h3 in order. Never jump (no h1 → h3, no h4 straight under a card title).
- Never pick a level for its size. Need a different look? Use a class.
- Popovers and menus: a title is `<h2 class="card-title">`; a person's name or other label is not a heading.
- Do not reintroduce the old long-form sizes (2.5rem h1, 1.5rem h4) on UI headings.
